specs/011-settings-dashboard/spec.md:52:3. **Given** the confirmation dialog is open, **When** the user taps "Apagar tudo", **Then** the app requests the account's permanent deletion, and on success clears all local session and account state and leaves the user at the app's authentication entry point, with no "account deleted" success screen of its own.
specs/011-settings-dashboard/spec.md:80:- The user double-taps "Apagar tudo" or "Sair" before the first request resolves: this does not fire a second concurrent delete/logout request.
specs/011-settings-dashboard/spec.md:105:- **FR-017**: Settings MUST offer an "Apagar conta" action (styled as destructive/red) that opens a confirmation dialog matching the prototype — red title "Apagar sua conta?", text stating the action is permanent and irreversible, a red "Apagar tudo" button, and an outline "Cancelar" button — and MUST NOT call the delete endpoint before this dialog is explicitly confirmed.
specs/011-settings-dashboard/spec.md:110:- **FR-022**: Repeated taps on "Sair" or "Apagar tudo" before a prior request for the same action resolves MUST NOT fire a second concurrent request.
specs/011-settings-dashboard/spec.md:138:- **Where "Sair" and "Apagar tudo" land**: The prototype extract states both actions return to the "Biometria" screen with no dedicated success screen of their own. Since both actions end with no stored session, and F000 already routes a device with no stored session to the login/sign-up screen on next launch, this unit treats "the app's authentication entry point" as whatever F000/RF03 already resolve that case to (the vault screen if a device-level PIN/biometric flow applies with no session, falling through to login otherwise) rather than building a separate destination.
